# Xibalba behind Caddy.
#
# Caddy obtains the certificate and passes every request to Xibalba, which
# listens on 127.0.0.1:8080. Change the site name. Caddy tells Xibalba the
# visitor's address and that the visitor came over HTTPS by itself, and
# passes websockets through; nothing more is needed.
#
# In xibalba.yaml, tell Xibalba to believe this Caddy:
#
#   server:
#     trusted_proxies: ["127.0.0.1"]
#
# Tested with Caddy 2.6 by test/webserver/check.py.

www.example.org {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8080
}
